course: dictionary
lesson: 4725
title: Word parts and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts, and each part is a clue. «Split «hopelessness» and it is just hope + less + ness.» Hope is a wish that good things will happen. Less means without, and ness turns a word into a noun, a name for a state or feeling.
explain: Put the parts together and hopelessness means the feeling of having no hope, or no chance of success. Test it in a sentence: «The villagers faced famine, and a sense of hopelessness settled over them.» Does your meaning still make sense there? Then it is right.
explain: Stories often show hopelessness in hard times, such as war, famine or being lost. Characters often find hope again, and that is part of the story. If you ever feel hopelessness yourself, talk to a trusted adult. Help is always available.
fact: Hopelessness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some hopelessness, not two hopelessnesses.
fact: Hope + less + ness: hope, less (without) and ness (a state or feeling).
fact: «Hopelessness» means a feeling that nothing good will happen and there is no point in trying.
fact: Common phrases are a feeling of hopelessness and a sense of hopelessness.
fact: Feelings of hopelessness are a sign to talk to a trusted adult, because help is always available.
exercise: Split hopelessness into parts. What does the part less mean? | Happy | *Without | Very | Again
exercise: «Her hopelessness grew as the rain kept falling.» What does hopelessness mean here? | A fast race to the finish | A bright, sunny feeling | *A feeling that nothing good will happen | A feeling of being full of food
exercise: Hopelessness is a noun. Which word is an adjective, not a noun? | *hopeless | hopefulness | hopelessness | hopelessly
test: «The villagers faced famine, and a sense of hopelessness settled over them.» What does hopelessness mean here? | *Feeling there is no chance of things getting better | Feeling brave and excited for a race | Feeling very full after a big meal | Feeling sleepy on a warm afternoon
test: If you feel hopelessness yourself, what is the best next step? | Keep it secret and never mention it | Wait for a storm to pass | Try to hide it from everyone for ever | *Find a trusted adult and talk to them
exam: What does the part ness do in hopelessness? | It means without | It means hope again | *It turns the word into a noun for a state or feeling | It makes the word a question
